  <knowledge>
    - Used abilities are announced as `<Name> uses <Fähigkeitsname>(<Fähigkeitslevel>)`.
    - If Runa or a monster gains focus (ΔFP > 0) the game outputs `<Name> gains <FP> focus`.
    - Each monster shows the next ability to be attempted as `<AbilityName>(<AbilityLevel>)`; this
  shows the next ability in the list without availability check.
    - Damage lines use the format `<Name> takes <Schaden>` where `<Schaden>` is `n phy. damage` or
  `n mag. damage`.
    - If an ability uses a die, the game requests the die roll using the `Enter dice roll [1--<d>]:`
   prompt.
    - The game separates overview output lines with 40 minus signs for readability.
    - All input value ranges are closed and inclusive (e.g., 1..n, 1..d, up to 2147483647).
    - The exact prompt string for seeds is: `Enter seeds [1--2147483647] separated by comma:`
    - The exact prompt string for selecting exactly one option is: `Enter number [1--<n>]:`
    - The exact prompt string for selecting multiple options is: `Enter numbers [1--<n>] separated
  by comma:`
    - The exact prompt string for dice rolls is: `Enter dice roll [1--<d>]:`
    - When offering healing, output the prompt 'Runa (current/max HP) can discard ability cards for
  healing (or none)'; empty input means no healing.
    - For level n the first ability in the list can be Slash(n) and the last can be Lightning(n).
    - Only the final damage after defensive reductions is printed.
    - Hit points and focus points are displayed as `<current>/<max>`.
    - If there is more than one monster and the chosen ability is offensive, the game asks for a
  target; if only one monster or a defensive ability, no target prompt is shown.
    - Valid seed values are in the interval [1, 2147483647].
    - The second seed is used to shuffle the monster cards of the current game level; order follows
  the monster tables for levels 1 and 2.
    - The focus output decision is based on the difference between original and new focus points
  (ΔFP).
  </knowledge>
